# Kanban bug cards

When a feature file has frontmatter `labels` including **`bug`** (case-insensitive), follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Bug cards.

## User provides

- `## Steps to Reproduce`
- `## Current Behavior` (legacy: `## What happens`)
- `## Expected Behavior`
- `## Feature Areas`
- `## QA Review` (during Review, if follow-up issues found)

## Agent provides (pre-implementation card review, before `in-progress`)

- `## Root Cause (current code)` — after reading Label Paths / codebase
- `## Acceptance Criteria` — testable fix bullets
- `## Out of Scope` — optional
- `## Label Paths` — resolved from Feature Areas via `docs/feature-areas.yaml`
- `## Corrective Action` — concrete fix plan (**not** `## Decisions`)

## Do not

- Use `## Decisions` on bug cards — use `## Corrective Action`
- Start implementation with empty or disputed **Corrective Action**
- Move to **Review** without all **Acceptance Criteria** marked `[x]`

## Full workflow

See `.cursor/skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md` for lifecycle, registry updates, and pytest gates.
